  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscS&E 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After testing several compounds in the lab, a research team has identified
    a potential cancer drug that will be moving into animal studies soon.


    <b>Before
    animal studies can begin, the Institutional Review Board (IRB) must review the
    study plan and approve it.</b>


    <b>Is this true or false?</b>'
  explanation: "An IRB is a committee that reviews and approves research that involves
    humans\u2014not laboratory or animal studies\u2014because its main job is to
    protect people who volunteer for research studies. Animal research is instead
    reviewed by a separate committee that focuses on animal welfare and safety: Institutional
    Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC). IRB review happens later, before any human
    clinical trials begin."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
